On October 9th 2026 we got hit with the following announcement:

> [https://deno.com/blog/cloudflare](https://deno.com/blog/cloudflare)
> 
> [https://blog.cloudflare.com/deno-joins-cloudflare/](https://blog.cloudflare.com/deno-joins-cloudflare/)

First thing I would like to get out of the way is that I am perfectly aware that few people were as emotionally invested in Deno as a project as I was, mainly because **Deno 1** never really took off and that diminished the geeral public's exposure to how great **Deno 2** was, fine, it doesn't matter that it never reached widespread adoption, many do agree it was great quality software and a good direction for the JS/TS ecosystem.

## The Announcement

> ...
> 
> Joining also means choosing where to focus our effort. We’ve decided to put our future development work into this shared platform rather than continuing to develop a separate runtime and hosting service. We know this is a consequential change for people who have built on Deno.
> 
> ...
